            "review_title": "Review at 5th avenue",
            "review_text": "GTranThanh\nParis, France1 contribution\n0\nMost amazing pasta in Hanoi\nMay 2012 • Friends\nMy name is Guillaume and I am coming from the France for 2 weeks vacation in Vietnam. A friend of mine told me that an Italian American just opened in the highest tower of Vietnam Keangnam. They do there home made pasta. It was incredibly difficult to find the restaurant as it was based in the 8th floor of the office tower (the highest one). After 10 minutes seeking for the restaurant I was very surprised to find a very cozy restaurant with a nice design. I ordered tagliatelle carbonara and I was amazed by the food. Pasta were home made like the ones we could find in fine grocery shopping shop. It was not very crowdy so the service was quite good and the bill very cheap. I paid 8 bucks for the meal per pax. I recommend his place to people who love pasta.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 13, 2012",
